MALPRACTICE AND PRODUCT LIABILITY LAWYERS HAVE FIELD DAY AT THE EXPENSE OF ARTIFICIAL HEART MANUFACTURER

@CORPFULL, maker of the "Energizer" human heart prosthesis, has become a clay pigeon for product liability lawyers and their clients, as a result of recently disclosed defects of a disastrous nature in the thousands of Energizers that have been implanted in human patients. Over 50% of such patients have already died, due to the tendency of the artificial hearts to stop working during electrical storms or when in close proximity to radios, TV sets or computers. Heart surgeons who have implanted the defective devices are also being sued in record numbers for medical malpractice, and as a result are themselves suing @CORPFULL.

